
## 1. Dielectric under an L2 window (RO4835 core + filled L2 copper + pressed RO4450F)
  bondply 90 um -> window dielectric 209 um (board_calc used 203 um)
  bondply 102 um -> window dielectric 221 um (board_calc used 203 um)

## 2. Patch centre-frequency uncertainty on the 8 mil window (fixed copper, nominal W 1.605 / L 1.192 mm)
  Dk +-0.10 (process 3.33-3.48 vs design 3.66; 60 GHz unknown)   +-0.76 GHz
  L etch +-13 um (LDI, good lot)                                 +-0.58 GHz
  L etch +-25 um (+-1 mil class)                                 +-1.13 GHz
  thickness +-10 %                                               +-0.59 GHz
  f0 nominal 61.73 GHz (model); RSS +-1.13 GHz (13 um etch) / +-1.49 GHz (25 um etch) = +-1.8 / +-2.4 %; patch BW 4.3 % = +-1.33 GHz
  bracketing step that covers +-RSS(13 um) with 3 variants: L scale +-1.8 %

## 3. Corporate 2-patch column inside one column pitch (d = 2.342 mm)
  W 1.250: gap 1.092 mm; 50-ohm 4 mil line 0.200 mm centred ->  446 um to each patch edge (2.10 h_window)
  W 1.250: gap 1.092 mm; 50-ohm 8 mil line 0.443 mm centred ->  325 um to each patch edge (1.53 h_window)
  W 1.400: gap 0.942 mm; 50-ohm 4 mil line 0.200 mm centred ->  371 um to each patch edge (1.75 h_window)
  W 1.400: gap 0.942 mm; 50-ohm 8 mil line 0.443 mm centred ->  250 um to each patch edge (1.18 h_window)
  W 1.605: gap 0.737 mm; 50-ohm 4 mil line 0.200 mm centred ->  269 um to each patch edge (1.27 h_window)
  W 1.605: gap 0.737 mm; 50-ohm 8 mil line 0.443 mm centred ->  147 um to each patch edge (0.69 h_window)
  W/L for W 1.25 / L 1.19 = 1.05: TM10 within ~5 % of TM01 -> cross-pol risk; keep W/L >= 1.2

## 4. Feed-loss bands carrying the model's own +-30 % conductor-loss error and a through-via launch
  RX 2.7 mm 4 mil                                      line 0.46 dB -> 0.6-1.4 dB (launch 0.3-0.8 dB)
  TX option B (1.5 mm 4 mil + 9.5 mm 8 mil + step)     line 1.16 dB -> 1.2-2.4 dB (launch 0.3-0.8 dB)
  TX all 4 mil GCPW (+10..20 % coplanar)               line 2.14 dB -> 1.8-3.6 dB (launch 0.3-0.8 dB)

## 5. 1.0 V RF/PA rail worst case at 2.5 A peak (window 0.95-1.05 V, SWRS219F 7.4)
  one ferrite carries 2.5 A, 5 mOhm shunt (plan)          IR 65.5 mV; worst-case min 0.884 V; nominal setpoint, half the step spec 0.919 V
  PA branch ferrite 2.0 A, 2 mOhm shunt (ISK Rev D style) IR 48.0 mV; worst-case min 0.902 V; nominal setpoint, half the step spec 0.937 V
  two ferrites in parallel on the PA branch, 2 mOhm       IR 28.0 mV; worst-case min 0.922 V; nominal setpoint, half the step spec 0.957 V

## 6. REG-01 off-time: where can a calibration/monitor emission of c ms go? (4.80 ms burst / 50 ms frame)
  inter-burst gap 45.2 ms; isolating an emission from both bursts needs >= 2 x 33 ms = 66 ms of gap -> impossible
  any emission shares a 33 ms window with a burst: burst + emission + sub-2 ms fragments <= 5.5 ms -> extra <= 0.70 ms
  alternatives: append <= 0.70 ms contiguous to the burst, or run cal/monitors in a frame that replaces one burst (<= 5.5 ms)

## 7. EIRP bound for the 2-patch column (directivity, not a measurement)
  2 isotropic elements at 0.55 lambda0: +3.4 dB; with a 6.5-7.0 dBi patch -> column 9.4-9.9 dBi (0.5 dB allowance for element-pattern overlap)
  2 isotropic elements at 0.60 lambda0: +3.7 dB; with a 6.5-7.0 dBi patch -> column 9.7-10.2 dBi (0.5 dB allowance for element-pattern overlap)
  -> use 10 dBi as the pre-measurement bound: TDM <= +2 dBm per port, 3-TX coherent <= -7.5 dBm per port (EIRP 12 dBm)

## 8. Via fence pitch and GSG coupon pitch (PCBWay 0.10 mm min space, 0.15 mm min drill)
  via 0.20/0.40: at 0.36 mm pitch pad gap -40 um; min pitch for 0.10 mm pad gap 0.50 mm
  via 0.15/0.35: at 0.36 mm pitch pad gap +10 um; min pitch for 0.10 mm pad gap 0.45 mm
  via 0.15/0.30: at 0.36 mm pitch pad gap +60 um; min pitch for 0.10 mm pad gap 0.40 mm
  lambda_g/8 = 0.37 mm (4 mil); a 0.45 mm pitch leaves 0.30 mm openings = lambda_g/10
  GSG 150 um with 0.10 mm pads: S-G copper gap 50 um (below 0.10 mm rule)
  GSG 200 um with 0.10 mm pads: S-G copper gap 100 um (ok)
  GSG 250 um with 0.10 mm pads: S-G copper gap 150 um (ok)

## 9. Thermal at 50 C ambient (RthJA 22.3 C/W is JEDEC 2S2P 76x114 mm, free air)
  1.0 W: JEDEC 72 C; small board in enclosure 30-40 C/W [E] -> 80-90 C (TJ max 105 C)
  1.3 W: JEDEC 79 C; small board in enclosure 30-40 C/W [E] -> 89-102 C (TJ max 105 C)
  1.5 W: JEDEC 83 C; small board in enclosure 30-40 C/W [E] -> 95-110 C (TJ max 105 C)

## 10. Corner-reflector far field (2 D^2 / lambda, D = aperture ~ a*sqrt(2))
  edge 48.6 mm: far field >= 2.0 m
  edge 27.3 mm: far field >= 0.6 m

## 11. TX length equalization geometry (option B arcs R >= 1.5 mm on 8 mil)
  TX1: Manhattan 4.00 mm -> extra +6.9 mm to reach 10.9 mm
  TX2: Manhattan 7.64 mm -> extra +3.3 mm to reach 10.9 mm
  TX3: Manhattan 11.28 mm -> extra -0.4 mm to reach 10.9 mm
  TX1 meander, 8 mil microstrip, R 1.5 mm: one period adds 3.42 mm + 2 x leg over 6.0 mm advance; +6.9 mm needs leg 1.74 mm -> about 6.0 x 5.2 mm of area
  TX1 meander, 4 mil GCPW, R 0.6 mm: one period adds 1.37 mm + 2 x leg over 2.4 mm advance; +6.9 mm needs leg 2.77 mm -> about 2.4 x 4.8 mm of area
  delay-match limit 7.9 ps = 1.40 mm (8 mil) / 1.44 mm (4 mil)
